From 5094421d9586294b2aad09924b9a54e2e6060f06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taewook Kim <chatmate@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 16:59:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Fix hanja table loading on Windows (MSVC text-mode
 ftell drift)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On Windows with MSVC, opening a file in text mode and using ftell() to
record key-block offsets produces incorrect values when the file uses
LF-only line endings. MSVC text mode assumes CRLF (2 bytes/newline),
so ftell() over-counts preceding newlines by 1 byte each. fseek() then
lands in the middle of a key block instead of at the start, and
hanja_table_seek_key() immediately fails the comparison, returning
0 hanja candidates for most hangul syllables.

Fix: open the hanja data file in binary mode (fopen "rb") so that
ftell() and fseek() agree on raw byte positions. On Linux/macOS, text
mode and binary mode are equivalent for LF-only files, so this is a
no-op on those platforms.

Tested on Windows 11 + MSVC via a standalone C harness:
before fix: 기/한/살 = 0 candidates; after fix: 307/100/17 candidates.

https://github.com/libhangul/libhangul/pull/103
---
 hangul/hanja.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hangul/hanja.c b/hangul/hanja.c
index 7812813..feb8eb9 100644
--- a/hangul/hanja.c
+++ b/hangul/hanja.c
@@ -501,7 +501,7 @@ hanja_table_load(const char* filename)
 	return NULL;
 #endif /* LIBHANGUL_DEFAULT_HANJA_DIC */
 
-    file = fopen(filename, "r");
+    file = fopen(filename, "rb");
     if (file == NULL) {
 	return NULL;
     }
-- 
2.55.0

From 21c2931a8a5d78d538aa648e23cc21b3ffc3d363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Choe Hwanjin <choe.hwanjin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:42:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Handle malformed hanja dictionary files (#106)

Avoid a NULL pointer dereference when parsing records without
a value field.

Replace strtok_r() with strpbrk() because strtok_r() cannot handle
consecutive delimiters correctly. Do not use strsep() because it
is not supported on Windows.

Fix a bug that prevented dictionaries containing a single entry
from being loaded, discovered while adding tests.

A bug in handling dictionaries with no entries was also found
and will be fixed in a separate commit.

https://github.com/libhangul/libhangul/issues/106
---
 hangul/hanja.c | 64 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hangul/hanja.c b/hangul/hanja.c
index feb8eb9..aa7848f 100644
--- a/hangul/hanja.c
+++ b/hangul/hanja.c
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #else
 #include <io.h>
-#define strtok_r strtok_s
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_MMAP
@@ -437,10 +436,32 @@ hanja_table_match(const HanjaTable* table,
 	fseek(table->file, offset, SEEK_SET);
 
 	while (fgets(buf, sizeof(buf), table->file) != NULL) {
-	    char* save = NULL;
-	    char* p = strtok_r(buf, ":", &save);
-	    res = strcmp(p, key);
-	    if (res == 0) {
+            char* k = buf;
+            char* p = strpbrk(k, ":");
+            if (p == NULL) {                    // no key
+                break;
+            }
+
+            p[0] = '\0';
+            p++;
+
+            res = strcmp(k, key);
+            if (res == 0) {
+                char* value = p;
+                p = strpbrk(value, ":");
+                if (p == NULL || p == value) {  // no value
+                    break;
+                }
+
+                p[0] = '\0';
+                p++;
+
+                char* comment = p;
+                p = strpbrk(comment, "\r\n");
+                if (p != NULL) {
+                    p[0] = '\0';
+                }
+
                 if (*list == NULL) {
                     *list = hanja_list_new(key);
                 }
@@ -449,12 +470,8 @@ hanja_table_match(const HanjaTable* table,
                     break;
                 }
 
-		char* value   = strtok_r(NULL, ":", &save);
-		char* comment = strtok_r(NULL, "\r\n", &save);
-
-		Hanja* hanja = hanja_new(p, value, comment);
-
